hands-desktop
Part of Mycroft (https://github.com/kurkavojtech/mycroft), MIT License, see ../LICENSE.

hands-desktop ports the Accessibility reading and acting of jev-use (https://github.com/savka777/jev-use) by Savva
Bojko, from Sources/JevDesktop/Desktop.swift. The ported code is in Sources/DesktopCore/AX/ (AXSupport.swift,
AXTree.swift, AXActions.swift and AXBackend.swift): reading the AX tree and building elements with roles, labels,
values, places and verbs; choosing operations; pressing, selecting, clicking, focusing, typing with unicode key events,
keys, scrolling and menus; opening apps, folders and URLs; and the before/after screen fingerprint. It was changed to
produce the JSON contract of docs/desktop-protocol.md (refs, places and operations instead of Jev candidates), to
report the protocol's error codes, to press menus by path, to scroll a screen at a time, and to refuse secure input.
jev-use's voice, speech, hotkey, Jev and planner parts are not used. jev-use is used under the following license:

